<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bihać</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bihać is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> on the Una river, near the Croatian border. A royal free town of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1592. In 1942 it hosted the first session of the Yugoslav partisans' council <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-fascist-council-for-the-national-liberation-of-yugoslavia">AVNOJ</a>, and in the 1990s it was besieged as the Bihać pocket.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bihac.jpg" alt="Bihać" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Nyča · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biha%C4%87_%E2%80%93_Kapetanova_kula.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
